# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context - the tarball the
# daemon receives before the first instruction runs. It is not a detail: the
# context is uploaded in full on every build, and anything inside it can be
# copied into an image by an accidental `COPY . .`.
#
# Deny nothing by default would mean sending 1.4 GB of virtual environment to
# build an image that rebuilds it anyway.

# The local virtual environment: 1.4 GB, built for this machine, and rebuilt
# inside the image from uv.lock. Copying it in would also be wrong, not merely
# slow - it holds absolute paths and binaries compiled for the host.
.venv/

# Secrets. Never in an image: an image is pushed, pulled, cached and scanned by
# people who are not you. Configuration reaches a container at RUN time,
# through the environment, never at BUILD time through a file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Caches and generated artefacts: large, machine-specific, and regenerated.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# User documents and the vector store live in a volume, not in an image.
../.data/
.data/

# Not needed to RUN the service. Tests belong in CI, which runs against the
# source, not against the production image. Shipping them enlarges the image
# and the attack surface for no benefit.
tests/
evals/

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
